.\" syncon.1 — SynthOmnicon CLI man page
.\" Generated 2026-03-19.  Format: groff -man  |  man -l syncon.1
.\"
.TH SYNCON 1 "2026\-03\-19" "SynthOmnicon 0.4.4" "SynthOmnicon User Commands"
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH NAME
syncon \- SynthOmnicon unified command\-line interface for synthonic system analysis
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syncon
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR]...
.br
.B synthomnicon
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR]...
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B syncon
(alias
.BR synthomnicon )
is the command\-line interface to the SynthOmnicon framework — a formal
algebra for encoding, analysing, and designing self\-organising systems across
molecular, supramolecular, temporal, quantum, and cross\-domain scales.
.PP
Every system is represented as a
.I synthon tuple
over ten primitives:
.PP
.RS 4
\fB⟨D\fR; \fBT\fR; \fBR\fR; \fBP\fR; \fBF\fR; \fBK\fR; \fBG\fR; \fBΓ\fR; \fBΦ\fR; \fBΩ⟩\fR
.RE
.PP
where
.B D
= dimensionality,
.B T
= topology,
.B R
= recognition mode,
.B P
= polarity,
.B F
= fidelity,
.B K
= kinetic character,
.B G
= granularity,
.B Γ
= interaction grammar,
.B Φ
= criticality phase, and
.B Ω
= topological protection index (optional).
.PP
The catalog ships with 223+ curated synthons spanning chemistry, protein
biology, condensed matter, gravity theories, and programmable matter.
User-defined synthons can be registered interactively or via
.BR generate (1)
and
.BR run (1).
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the framework version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a brief usage summary and exit.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH COMMANDS
Commands are grouped by function below.
All commands accept
.B \-\-help
for detailed usage.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS Catalog Management
.TP
.B syncon catalog list
List all registered synthons (name, domain, fidelity, Φ_c flag).
.TP
.B syncon catalog repair
Batch\-repair systematic misassignments in the catalog.
.TP
.B syncon catalog auto\-stoichiometry
Backfill stoichiometry on T⋈ entries that have none.
.TP
.B syncon catalog rebuild\-index
Rebuild the analogy engine index from live catalog state.
.TP
.BI "syncon export " "[\-f json|csv|yaml]  [\-o FILE]  [\-d DOMAIN]"
Export the catalog to a file in the specified format.
.TP
.BI "syncon remove " NAME " [NAME ...]"
Remove one or more synthons from the catalog by name.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS Inspection and Comparison
.TP
.BI "syncon analyze " IDENTIFIER
Display all primitive fields, axiom status, Φ_c score, and grounding
metadata for a synthon.
.I IDENTIFIER
may be a catalog name or a raw notation string
.IR ⟨D_wedge;\ ...⟩ .
Supports
.BR \-f " text|json|notation."
.TP
.BI "syncon compare " "SYNTHON [SYNTHON ...] [\-g ΔG ...] [\-\-include\-thermo]"
Display a side-by-side primitive table for two or more synthons.
Optional ΔG values enable thermodynamic comparison.
.TP
.BI "syncon check " "SYNTHON_A SYNTHON_B"
Check compatibility (D/T/R/P match, F\-floor ordering, ξ_CP delta) between
two synthons.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS Lattice Algebra
.TP
.BI "syncon meet " "SYNTHON_A SYNTHON_B"
Lattice MEET (⊓) — greatest lower bound of two synthons.
Ordered primitives (F, K, G) take the minimum; categorical conflicts are
flagged.
Useful for identifying the minimal common precursor motif.
.TP
.BI "syncon join " "SYNTHON_A SYNTHON_B"
Lattice JOIN (⊔) — least upper bound of two synthons.
Ordered primitives take the maximum; categorical conflicts are flagged.
Returns the specification a scaffold must satisfy to host both components.
.TP
.BI "syncon tensor " "SYNTHON_A SYNTHON_B [\-\-lambda FLOAT]"
Tensor product s₁ ⊗ s₂ — predicts the primitive profile of the combined
assembly.
D takes the union; T is topology-promoted; F/K take the minimum (bottleneck);
G takes the maximum.
.B \-\-lambda
controls mutual\-information discounting (default 0.3).
.TP
.BI "syncon lift " "SYNTHON TARGET"
Apply a natural transformation (dimensional lift) to a synthon.
.I TARGET
is one of
.BR temporal ", " spatial ", " critical ", or " molecular .
The
.B critical
lift injects Φ_c and requires F ≥ F_ℏ.
.TP
.BI "syncon distance " "SYNTHON_A SYNTHON_B [\-\-directed]"
Compute the weighted quasi\-metric tuple distance.
Default is symmetric (Hamming\-like over all ten primitives).
.B \-\-directed
mode penalises downward F/K moves (HotSwap floor semantics).
.TP
.BI "syncon path " "SOURCE DESTINATION [\-\-max\-hops N] [\-\-xi\-tol FLOAT]"
Find the shortest valid HotSwap path from
.I SOURCE
to
.I DESTINATION
through the catalog.
Path edges are restricted to synthons sharing D and T.
Edge weight = |ΔξCP| per hop; BFS minimises hop count.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS Decomposition Algebra
The decomposition module implements the
.I inverse
of the build\-up operations, enabling retrosynthetic analysis of any synthon.
.TP
.BI "syncon project " "SYNTHON PRIM [PRIM ...]"
Project a synthon onto a named subset of primitives, zeroing all others.
.I PRIM
tokens are field names from the set
.BR F ", " K ", " G ", " D ", " T ", " R ", " P ", " Phi ", " Omega ", " Gamma .
.TP
.BI "syncon peel " "SYNTHON PRIM [\-\-strict]"
Descend one tier on a single primitive.
Returns the resulting synthon and the peel cost in nats.
.B \-\-strict
blocks the peel if it would destroy Φ_c (phase protection).
Phi removal costs 3.0 nats; ordinal peel of F/K/G costs 0 unless Φ_c is
thereby destroyed.
.TP
.BI "syncon factor " "SYNTHON [\-\-prefer PRIM]"
Find the strongest meet\-irreducible factor of a synthon — the sub\-synthon
that best characterises its dominant structure.
.B \-\-prefer
biases the factoring toward a named primitive.
.TP
.BI "syncon principal\-decomp " SYNTHON
Recursively factor a synthon down to its join\-irreducible atoms.
The principal decomposition reveals the minimal building blocks whose lattice
join reproduces the full synthon.
Quantum gravity decomposes into 8 atoms; the standard model into 3.
.TP
.BI "syncon cofactor " "COMPOSITE FACTOR_A"
Compute the cofactor residual B such that FACTOR_A ⊗ B ≈ COMPOSITE.
Per\-primitive roles are reported: CONTRIBUTOR (B must supply), BOTTLENECK
(A is the limiting floor), CONFLICT (irreconcilable mismatch), EXPLAINED
(fully covered by A), or PASSTHROUGH (categorical difference, forwarded).
A D\-CONFLICT in
.B cofactor(QG, GR)
is the algebraic form of the background\-dependence problem.
.TP
.BI "syncon retrosyn " "TARGET [\-\-top N] [\-\-max\-factors N]"
Retrosynthetic search: find catalog entries (or pairs) whose tensor product
most closely approaches
.IR TARGET .
Results are ranked by tuple distance.
The fractional quantum Hall state
.RB ( fqh_moore_read )
is the closest single\-synthon approximation to quantum gravity in the
current catalog (d = 3.1).
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS HotSwap and Design Validation
.TP
.BI "syncon hotswap " "TARGET CANDIDATE [\-g ΔG] [\-\-allow\-defect\-fraction FLOAT]"
Validate a synthon hot\-swap using the full HotSwap protocol.
Enforces D/T/S exact match, F_new ≥ F_old, |Δξ_CP| < 1.0 nat, K
accessibility, and grounding status.
Runs the Varma QXY probe automatically when Φ_c is suspected.
.TP
.BI "syncon transition " "SRC DST [\-\-max\-hops N] [\-\-xi\-tolerance FLOAT]"
Classify the phase transition between two catalog synthons.
Reports whether the transition is 2nd\-order (continuous HotSwap path through
Φ_c intermediates) or 1st\-order (no valid path due to structural conflict).
Forward/reverse costs and irreversibility asymmetry are displayed.
.TP
.BI "syncon pipeline " "START_SYNTHON \-\-step OP:ARG [...]"
Chain algebra operations into a composable design pipeline.
Implements Writer + Maybe monad semantics: each step threads ξ_CP deltas and
warnings; the pipeline short\-circuits on the first blocking failure.
Step operators:
.B meet:SYNTHON\fR,
.B join:SYNTHON\fR,
.B tensor:SYNTHON[:lambda=0.3]\fR,
.B lift:TARGET\fR,
.B path:TARGET[:max_hops=6,xi_tol=1.0]\fR.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS Analysis and Probes
.TP
.BI "syncon thermo " "IDENTIFIER [\-g ΔG] [\-t TEMP]"
Calculate thermodynamic efficiency metrics ηCP and ξCP for a synthon.
ΔG defaults to reference values from the catalog where available.
.TP
.BI "syncon criticality " "[SYNTHON_NAME | \-\-all] [\-\-min\-confidence FLOAT]"
Analyse synthon criticality via G\-D degeneracy scoring.
.B \-\-all
scans the full catalog and returns a ranked candidate list.
.TP
.BI "syncon criticality\-probe " "[ENTRY_NAME] [\-\-batch] [\-\-xi\-r FLOAT] [\-\-xi\-tau FLOAT]"
Probe a catalog entry for Φ_c candidacy using four checks: G/D degeneracy
independence score, Varma QXY scaling (requires \-\-xi\-r / \-\-xi\-tau),
recursive tuple potential, and Φ_c likelihood score (0–1).
.TP
.BI "syncon info\-bits " "[ENTRY_NAME] [\-\-solvent] [\-\-calibrate]"
Compute rigorous I(bits) via degree\-of\-freedom counting.
Decomposes information content into I_recognition, I_orientation, and
I_net = I_recognition − 0.3 × I_orientation.
Default range: 6–18 bits (domain\-dependent).
.TP
.BI "syncon perturb sweep " "SYNTHON [\-g ΔG]"
Compute the Primitive Jacobian ∂ξ_CP/∂p over all ten primitives (one tier
perturbation each).
Identifies the design lever with the largest distance impact.
.TP
.BI "syncon perturb fault\-injection " SYNTHON
Identify single points of failure (SPOF) — primitives whose one\-tier
downgrade causes the largest increase in ξ_CP or loss of Φ_c.
.TP
.BI "syncon phase\-diagram " "[NAME ...] [\-\-output FILE]"
Compute and render a tuple\-space phase diagram.
Detects phase boundaries as large jumps in pairwise tuple distance.
Renders a Ward dendrogram + MDS 2‑D phase map.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS Ensemble and Multi-Synthon
.TP
.BI "syncon ensemble check " "SYNTHON [SYNTHON ...]"
Check pairwise compatibility of ensemble components: D/T overlap, F/K
bottleneck propagation, and Φ_c join\-dominance.
.TP
.BI "syncon ensemble probe " "SYNTHON [SYNTHON ...]"
Scan for emergent properties arising only in composition — properties present
in the ensemble that are absent in every constituent.
.TP
.BI "syncon ensemble thermo " "SYNTHON [SYNTHON ...] [\-g ΔG ...]"
Compute system\-level ηCP / ξCP for the full assembly event.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS Retrodesign
.TP
.BI "syncon retrodesign " "TARGET [\-d DEPTH] [\-p AXIOMS] [\-\-strict\-grounding] [\-\-allow\-ktrap]"
Constraint\-directed retrosynthetic decomposition of a target notation.
Axiom\-pruned decomposition with LLM route ranking.
.I TARGET
is a catalog name or raw
.IR ⟨...⟩ " notation string."
.B \-p
accepts comma\-separated axiom numbers to enforce (default: 1,2,4,6).
Distinct from
.BR retrosyn :
.B retrodesign
performs axiom\-guided tree decomposition of the notation;
.B retrosyn
searches the catalog for tensor\-product pairs.
.TP
.BI "syncon trajectory validate " "CYCLE_FILE [\-\-strict]"
Validate continuity and Axiom 6 compliance for a D_∞ temporal cycle.
.TP
.BI "syncon trajectory criticality " CYCLE_FILE
Compute G/D degeneracy score per step to determine the per\-step Φ_c
contribution of a temporal pathway.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS Validation and Reasoning
.TP
.BI "syncon validate " SYNTHON_NAME
Validate a synthon against all composition axioms using the symbolic
reasoning engine.
Reports axiom pass/fail, G\-D independence analysis, criticality detection,
and predictive rule generation.
.TP
.BI "syncon analogies " "SYNTHON_NAME [\-\-critical\-only] [\-\-exclude\-flagged]"
Find formal cross\-domain analogies to a synthon using primitive similarity
metrics.
The framework encodes GR and the Standard Model as synthon tuples; this
command reveals which known systems share the same structural algebra.
.TP
.BI "syncon rules " "[\-\-min\-support N] [\-\-min\-confidence FLOAT]"
Discover inductive predictive rules from the catalog.
Returns IF\-THEN rules of the form: IF (T = T_bowtie AND P = P_±) THEN
(F ≥ F_ℏ).
.TP
.BI "syncon audit " "[\-\-fix] [\-\-limit N]"
Audit catalog entries for grounding issues.
Reports primitives lacking mechanistic justification.
.B \-\-fix
attempts automatic repair.
.TP
.BI "syncon reconstruct " "[OPTIONS]"
Back\-fill catalog reasoning from discovery history.
Useful after batch import or catalog migration.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS AI-Assisted Generation and Design
.TP
.BI "syncon generate " "DESCRIPTION [\-n NAME] [\-g ΔG] [\-s SMILES] [\-\-axiom\-guided] [\-\-require\-grounding] [\-\-strict\-grounding]"
Generate a synthon from a natural language description using an LLM.
With
.B \-\-axiom\-guided,
the agent iteratively refines until all five composition axioms are satisfied.
With
.B \-\-require\-grounding,
all primitive assignments must have mechanistic justifications.
.TP
.BI "syncon generate\-smiles " "SMILES [\-n NAME] [\-f GROUPS] [\-\-provider PROVIDER]"
Generate a synthon from a SMILES string.
RDKit estimates ΔG when available.
.TP
.BI "syncon design " "GOAL [\-\-target SYNTHON] [\-\-phi\-c\-min FLOAT] [\-\-xi\-cp\-max FLOAT]"
Autonomous relational design agent (LLM\-in\-the\-loop).
The agent proposes encodings, validates them against the axiom set, probes
Φ_c and ξ_CP, finds cross\-domain analogues, and self\-corrects until
convergence criteria are met (Φ_c score ≥
.B \-\-phi\-c\-min
AND ξ_CP ≤
.B \-\-xi\-cp\-max\fR).
With
.B \-\-target,
a HotSwap path to that catalog entry is also required.
.TP
.BI "syncon tool " "{validate|criticality|path|analogies|distance|meet|generate} [\-\-name SYNTHON] [...]"
Single\-shot SynthonTool dispatch — the LLM tool layer exposed directly on
the command line.
Every operation returns a structured result; axiom violations include a
precise primitive trace.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS DSL Runner
.TP
.BI "syncon run " SCRIPT
Evaluate a
.IR .syn
YAML design script as a typed SynthonM pipeline.
Step operations supported in the
.B do:
block:
.BR join , " meet" , " tensor" , " lift" , " path" , " assert" , " bind .
The monad threads ξ_CP deltas and short-circuits on axiom violations.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS Cache Management
.TP
.B syncon cache
Manage framework caches (LLM response cache, analogy index, phase diagram
data).
Subcommands:
.BR clear ", " status ", " rebuild .
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH PRIMITIVES
The ten primitives and their principal values:
.PP
.TS
l l .
\fBD\fR (Dimensionality)	MOLECULAR · SUPRAMOLECULAR · TEMPORAL · HOLOGRAPHIC
\fBT\fR (Topology)	LINEAR · CYCLIC · NETWORK · BRAID · BOWL · HUB · BOWTIE · CAGE
\fBR\fR (Recognition Mode)	NON_COVALENT · DYNAMIC_CATALYTIC · MECHANICAL · COVALENT_REVERSIBLE
\fBP\fR (Polarity)	SELF_COMPLEMENTARY_SYM · SELF_COMPLEMENTARY_PSEUDO · DONOR_ACCEPTOR
\fBF\fR (Fidelity)	HIGH (F_ℏ) · MEDIUM (F_eth) · LOW (F_ℓ)
\fBK\fR (Kinetic Character)	FAST · MODERATE · SLOW · TRAP · MBL
\fBG\fR (Granularity)	LOCAL (G_beth) · MESOSCALE (G_gimel) · GLOBAL (G_aleph)
\fBΓ\fR (Interaction Grammar)	SELECTIVE_AND · BROAD_OR · QUANTUM_AND · CATEGORICAL
\fBΦ\fR (Criticality Phase)	SUBCRITICAL · CRITICAL
\fBΩ\fR (Topological Index)	None · Z2_CLASS · CHERN · NON_ABELIAN (optional)
.TE
.PP
.B Ordinal primitives
(F, K, G) support inequality comparisons; the ordering from weakest to
strongest is LOW < MEDIUM < HIGH for F, FAST < MODERATE < SLOW < TRAP < MBL
for K, and LOCAL < MESOSCALE < GLOBAL for G.
.B Categorical primitives
(D, T, R, P, Γ) require exact match for compatibility; mismatches in
.B meet
and
.B cofactor
are reported as CONFLICT.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH NOTATION FORMAT
Synthon tuples are written in angle brackets:
.PP
.RS 4
.B ⟨D_wedge; T_bowtie; R_superset; P_pm_sym; F_hbar; K_mod; G_gimel; Gamma_and(SELECTIVE); Phi_c; Omega_Z2⟩
.RE
.PP
The symbols map to:
.B D_wedge
= SUPRAMOLECULAR,
.B T_bowtie
= BOWTIE,
.B R_superset
= NON_COVALENT,
.B P_pm_sym
= SELF_COMPLEMENTARY_SYM,
.B F_hbar
= HIGH,
.B F_eth
= MEDIUM,
.B F_ell
= LOW,
.B K_mod
= MODERATE,
.B K_trap
= TRAP,
.B G_beth
= LOCAL,
.B G_gimel
= MESOSCALE,
.B G_aleph
= GLOBAL,
.B Phi_c
= CRITICAL,
.B Phi_sub
= SUBCRITICAL.
.PP
Notation strings can be passed directly as the
.I IDENTIFIER
argument to
.B analyze
without prior catalog registration.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH AXIOMS
The framework enforces seven composition axioms at registration and
.B validate
time:
.TP
.BR "Axiom 1" " (G\-D compatibility)"
G and D must be mutually consistent: G_aleph requires D ≠ MOLECULAR.
.TP
.BR "Axiom 2" " (F\-floor ratchet)"
HotSwap paths may only increase F or hold it constant; F degradation is
blocked.
.TP
.BR "Axiom 3" " (K\-accessibility)"
K_trap may only be reached from K_slow; direct FAST → TRAP transitions are
blocked.
.TP
.BR "Axiom 4" " (Topology\-recognition compatibility)"
T_braid requires R ≠ COVALENT; T_cage requires F ≥ F_eth.
.TP
.BR "Axiom 5" " (G\-D degeneracy / Φ_c condition)"
Φ_c is valid when G and D span orthogonal scale classes — G/D degeneracy
signals a critical phase.
Extended Axiom 5: R degeneracy at G_aleph (ER=EPR condition).
.TP
.BR "Axiom 6" " (Grounding)"
Every primitive assignment in a registered synthon must carry a mechanistic
justification (for non\-discovery synthons).
.TP
.BR "Axiom 7" " (Stoichiometry consistency)"
T_bowtie (self\-complementary topology) requires P = SELF_COMPLEMENTARY_SYM
or SELF_COMPLEMENTARY_PSEUDO; stoichiometry ratio must match topology valency.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH EXAMPLES
.\"
.B Look up a synthon:
.RS 4
.B syncon analyze allosteric_domain
.RE
.PP
.B Compute the meet and tensor product of two synthons:
.RS 4
.B syncon meet carboxylic_acid_dimer adenine_thymine_pair
.br
.B syncon tensor standard_model general_relativity
.RE
.PP
.B Find the quantization residual B such that GR ⊗ B ≈ QG:
.RS 4
.B syncon cofactor quantum_gravity general_relativity
.RE
.PP
.B Decompose quantum gravity into join-irreducible atoms:
.RS 4
.B syncon principal\-decomp quantum_gravity
.RE
.PP
.B Find what AdS/CFT adds above GR (holography as a cofactor):
.RS 4
.B syncon cofactor ads_cft_boundary general_relativity
.RE
.PP
.B Retrosynthetic search for catalog pairs approaching quantum gravity:
.RS 4
.B syncon retrosyn quantum_gravity \-\-top 5
.RE
.PP
.B GNF-2 drug gap analysis (what does GNF-2 still lack vs. the allosteric domain?):
.RS 4
.B syncon cofactor allosteric_domain gnf_2
.RE
.PP
.B Peel the criticality phase layer from a condensate (strict mode):
.RS 4
.B syncon peel allosteric_domain Phi \-\-strict
.RE
.PP
.B Validate a proposed hot-swap candidate:
.RS 4
.B syncon hotswap proline_aldol_cycle allene_crown_catalyst
.RE
.PP
.B Identify the most impactful primitive lever (Jacobian sweep):
.RS 4
.B syncon perturb sweep allosteric_domain \-g \-45.0
.RE
.PP
.B Find the shortest HotSwap path between two protein domain synthons:
.RS 4
.B syncon path allosteric_domain active_site
.RE
.PP
.B Run a .syn design script:
.RS 4
.B syncon run my_design.syn
.RE
.PP
.B Classify the phase transition between condensate liquid and gel:
.RS 4
.B syncon transition condensate_liquid condensate_gel
.RE
.PP
.B Generate a synthon from a SMILES string:
.RS 4
.B syncon generate\-smiles "CC(=O)O" \-\-name acetic_acid
.RE
.PP
.B Launch the autonomous design agent:
.RS 4
.B syncon design "bivalent allosteric ABL inhibitor" \-\-target allosteric_domain \-\-phi\-c\-min 0.70
.RE
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
Most commands support
.B \-f text|json
(or
.B \-f text|json|notation
for
.BR analyze ).
JSON output is suitable for piping into
.BR jq (1)
or scripting.
.PP
.RS 4
.B syncon cofactor quantum_gravity general_relativity \-f json | jq '.dimensions[] | select(.role == "CONTRIBUTOR")'
.RE
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH FILES
.TP
.I synthomnicon/catalog.json
Default catalog storage path (relative to the project root, or as configured
via
.BR SYNTHONICON_CATALOG_PATH ).
.TP
.I *.syn
SynthonM design scripts.
YAML format evaluated by
.BR "syncon run" .
.TP
.I provider_defaults.yaml
LLM provider configuration for
.BR generate ", " design ", and " tool .
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SYNTHONICON_CATALOG_PATH
Override the default catalog file path.
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
Required for
.BR generate ", " design ", and " tool
when using the Anthropic provider.
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
Required when using the OpenAI provider.
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error (synthon not found, axiom violation, blocked HotSwap path,
parse error).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (missing required argument, unrecognised option).
.\"
.\" ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH NOTES
The
.B syncon
and
.B synthomnicon
entry points are identical aliases.
Both are registered at package install time via
.B pyproject.toml
console_scripts.
.PP
Φ_c (CRITICAL phase) is a
.I categorical
field, not derived from the ordinal primitives F, K, or G.
A synthon with F=LOW, K=FAST, G=LOCAL can carry Φ_c — see Prediction P\-49
in
.IR PRIMITIVE_PREDICTIONS.md .
.PP
The
.B cofactor
command implements the algebraic inverse of tensor.
.B cofactor(QG, GR)
reveals the background\-dependence problem as a D\-CONFLICT (P\-51).
.B cofactor(AdS/CFT, GR)
encodes holographic duality as the two-primitive operation
⟨G_GLOBAL ⊗ Φ_c⟩ (P\-54).
.PP
For the full theoretical derivation and axiom set, see
.I SYNTHONICON.md
in the project repository.
For all registered predictions, see
.IR PRIMITIVE_PREDICTIONS.md .
